WEBVTT

00:00.390 --> 00:03.874
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.875 --> 00:07.179
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.180 --> 00:10.751
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.752 --> 00:13.756
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.757 --> 00:17.261
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.262 --> 00:20.566
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.567 --> 00:22.136
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.137 --> 00:23.505
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.506 --> 00:29.946
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.356 --> 00:37.460
<i>We now return to Rational Geographic.</i>

00:37.461 --> 00:39.530
<i>Upon realizing a trip to Africa</i>

00:39.531 --> 00:41.032
<i>would be smelly and gross,</i>

00:41.033 --> 00:43.234
<i>our crew decided to stay in the office.</i>

00:49.346 --> 00:52.216
Aah! Mom, Dad! A bat, a bat!

00:52.217 --> 00:54.085
Oh, my God, there's a bat in the house.

00:54.086 --> 00:55.721
Okay, all-all right,
everybody just calm down,

00:55.722 --> 00:57.724
it might just be Grandpa Munster.

00:57.725 --> 00:59.294
Somebody set him up for a funny joke.

00:59.295 --> 01:00.795
Hey, Grandpa,

01:00.796 --> 01:03.433
how did you sleep last night?

01:03.434 --> 01:05.270
Yeah, see, if it was
him, he would have said,

01:05.271 --> 01:07.803
"Like I do every night: upside down."

01:09.043 --> 01:10.544
Okay. But Peter,

01:10.545 --> 01:12.581
we can't have a bat
flying around the house.

01:12.582 --> 01:13.984
We got to do something.

01:13.985 --> 01:15.686
Don't worry, Lois. I'll get rid of it.

01:15.687 --> 01:16.887
It'll be a piece of cake.

01:16.888 --> 01:18.858
Just like my penis enhancement.

01:18.859 --> 01:21.260
I want it to hang down to my knees.

01:22.583 --> 01:24.651
They moved up my knees.

01:28.473 --> 01:31.777
Everybody, I've come up with the
perfect plan to catch the bat.

01:31.778 --> 01:34.147
I bought this remote-
controlled toy helicopter,

01:34.148 --> 01:36.018
to which I have attached this handgun.

01:36.019 --> 01:38.488
And I tell you, this thing
is not easy to fly.

01:38.489 --> 01:40.424
- Peter, that doesn't seem very...
- Here goes.

01:40.425 --> 01:42.494
Now, I don't have anything
to control the trigger with,

01:42.495 --> 01:43.963
so I put it on a timer.

01:43.964 --> 01:45.833
But I don't remember
how long I set it...

01:45.834 --> 01:47.768
Aah! We're all gonna die!

01:50.474 --> 01:53.778
Okay, so, now the bat has a
gun, and the knives I gave him.

01:53.779 --> 01:55.348
What? Why would you give him knives?

01:55.349 --> 01:56.716
I didn't think it would matter.

01:56.717 --> 01:59.252
I was counting on this
helicopter thing working.

02:03.127 --> 02:05.263
Peter? Wh-where are you?

02:05.264 --> 02:06.498
What's going on?

02:06.499 --> 02:08.669
In order to understand the bat,

02:08.670 --> 02:11.606
we must first understand the vampire.

02:11.607 --> 02:14.144
<i>So I watched Interview With the Vampire.</i>

02:14.145 --> 02:16.147
Cast your gaze upon...

02:16.148 --> 02:17.816
Lestat.

02:17.817 --> 02:19.719
Peter, you're not a vampire.

02:19.720 --> 02:22.289
Oh? Then why am I clad in velvet pants

02:22.290 --> 02:24.493
tucked into soft leather boots?

02:24.494 --> 02:26.263
And why does my shirt billow so

02:26.264 --> 02:28.298
in the wind of that rotating fan?

02:28.299 --> 02:29.868
Peter, what's really going on?

02:29.869 --> 02:31.770
I'm just tryin' to reinvent my look.

02:31.771 --> 02:33.741
A guy at work said I dress like crap.

02:33.742 --> 02:36.088
Well, you show 'em tomorrow, Peter.

02:37.041 --> 02:38.214
How'd it go?

02:38.215 --> 02:40.584
I was sent home early and
labeled a distraction.

02:40.585 --> 02:42.621
They're having a meeting
about me tomorrow.

02:49.265 --> 02:50.667
Wha... Wh-What's wrong?

02:50.668 --> 02:53.270
Ar-Are we taking a
terrible 7:00 a.m. flight?

02:53.271 --> 02:54.941
No no. I realized to catch a bat,

02:54.942 --> 02:57.478
I need to live like a bat.
So I got to be up at night.

02:57.479 --> 02:59.381
It's a nocturnal mission, Lois.

02:59.382 --> 03:01.350
Okay, but what are you gonna do?

03:01.351 --> 03:02.552
Well, as everyone knows,

03:02.553 --> 03:05.023
bats watch a ton of
Cinemax softcore porn,

03:05.024 --> 03:06.961
so that seems like the place to start.

03:10.800 --> 03:12.167
A-ha!

03:12.168 --> 03:13.936
<i>Welcome back to CNBC's Moneyline.</i>

03:13.937 --> 03:15.939
Oh come on, man, nobody's buyin' that.

03:15.940 --> 03:17.709
You expect me to believe you own stocks?

03:17.710 --> 03:19.613
Bat Industries was up two
dollars a share today

03:19.614 --> 03:20.814
in heavy trading.

03:20.815 --> 03:22.015
Huh.

03:22.016 --> 03:24.386
Get back here! Damn it!

03:24.387 --> 03:26.222
Aah!

03:47.423 --> 03:49.992
I got you now, Bat Damon.

03:49.993 --> 03:51.929
I named you Bat Damon.

03:51.930 --> 03:54.165
Aw, now I want you to live.

03:55.635 --> 03:57.371
Aah! Aah! What is it?

03:57.372 --> 03:59.573
- Aah!
- Ow!

04:00.678 --> 04:04.248
You can beat me, but I am who I am!

04:04.249 --> 04:06.486
Peter, what the hell did
you do to Stewie's hand?

04:06.487 --> 04:07.854
It could be broken.

04:07.855 --> 04:09.390
I didn't mean to. It's just,

04:09.391 --> 04:11.925
sometimes I don't think before I act.

04:12.997 --> 04:14.291
Oh, hey, high-five.

04:14.746 --> 04:16.734
Hey, did you just high-five that sign?

04:16.735 --> 04:17.936
Yeah.

04:17.937 --> 04:19.539
You think differently.

04:19.540 --> 04:20.612
Get in.

04:24.747 --> 04:26.250
<i>His name was Derek.</i>

04:26.251 --> 04:28.753
<i>But he went by the Prophet
when times were good,</i>

04:28.754 --> 04:31.224
<i>or the Law Giver when times were bad.</i>

04:31.225 --> 04:34.061
<i>I moved onto his prayer
farm with 45 other members</i>

04:34.062 --> 04:37.500
<i>of the Salvation Star Boys,
who died in a mass suicide.</i>

04:37.501 --> 04:39.837
<i>But not me. 'Cause I
don't like root beer.</i>

04:39.838 --> 04:41.773
<i>And I only drink what I like.</i>

04:41.774 --> 04:44.578
<i>After it was all over, I
called Lois to pick me up.</i>

04:44.579 --> 04:46.146
<i>She was mad.</i>

04:46.147 --> 04:49.118
<i>But she's what Derek calls
an Oppressing Doubter.</i>

04:49.119 --> 04:51.088
<i>May the light of Derek's
Invincible Diamond</i>

04:51.089 --> 04:53.090
<i>shine through you.</i>

04:56.898 --> 04:59.769
Oh, thank you so much for
coming in early, Dr. Hartman.

04:59.770 --> 05:00.970
Oh, no problem.

05:00.971 --> 05:02.606
- Hell, I used to work here.
- What?

05:02.607 --> 05:04.843
Good news. Stewie's hand looks fine.

05:04.844 --> 05:06.679
Oh, hey, high-five.

05:06.680 --> 05:08.215
Huh. As long as you're here,

05:08.216 --> 05:10.318
I see Stewie hasn't had
his vaccinations yet.

05:10.319 --> 05:11.420
Should we take care of that?

05:11.421 --> 05:13.022
Well, I suppose so.

05:13.023 --> 05:15.326
Oh, but first, I'm required to
have you read this pamphlet

05:15.327 --> 05:17.428
about the risks of vaccinations.

05:20.535 --> 05:23.071
God, you are aging so rapidly.

05:23.072 --> 05:24.441
"Possible side effects:

05:24.442 --> 05:28.013
fever, severe allergic reaction,
muscle and joint pain?"

05:28.014 --> 05:29.414
Wait, and this can't be right:

05:29.415 --> 05:32.319
they actually put some of
the disease in the shot?

05:32.320 --> 05:34.456
Hey, man, how many
questions your lady ask?

05:34.457 --> 05:35.790
Uh, like, a million?

05:35.791 --> 05:37.694
But I don't remember
having to read any of this

05:37.695 --> 05:40.064
when Chris and Meg had
their vaccinations.

05:40.065 --> 05:41.800
Well, that was before
Internet chat rooms

05:41.801 --> 05:42.968
made everybody an expert.

05:42.969 --> 05:44.204
It's a better world now.

05:44.205 --> 05:46.708
I-I don't know about this, Dr. Hartman.

05:46.709 --> 05:49.245
We might need a little bit
of time to think this over.

05:49.246 --> 05:50.948
Yeah, 'cause we don't want
to make a big mistake.

05:50.949 --> 05:53.352
Like when I peed next to the chatty guy.

05:55.088 --> 05:56.189
Hey, man, we should get out of here,

05:56.190 --> 05:57.325
the building's on fire.

05:57.326 --> 05:58.794
Hey, pal, not now, I'm busy.

05:58.795 --> 06:01.832
Anyway, I'll tell you
what's on fire, my urethra.

06:01.833 --> 06:03.768
That's the last time I
go to a water park,

06:03.769 --> 06:04.869
I'll tell you that much.

06:04.870 --> 06:06.572
Well, that's not completely true,

06:06.573 --> 06:08.776
'cause I have a Groupon,
and I'd hate to waste it.

06:08.777 --> 06:10.045
Plus, the truth is, the kids...

06:10.046 --> 06:12.014
Oh, my God...

06:12.015 --> 06:14.818
<i>I was the chatty guy.</i>

06:19.593 --> 06:20.995
Hey, you guys, is that my laptop?

06:20.996 --> 06:23.098
Yeah, sorry, we were
looking something up.

06:23.099 --> 06:24.934
We were going to get Stewie vaccinated,

06:24.935 --> 06:28.006
but now, after our research,
we're definitely not.

06:28.007 --> 06:29.207
Ah, no, Lois, don't tell me

06:29.208 --> 06:31.378
you fell for all that anti-vaxxer crap.

06:31.379 --> 06:32.980
It's not crap, Brian.

06:32.981 --> 06:34.984
There's a lot of evidence
to suggest there's a link

06:34.985 --> 06:37.053
between vaccinations and autism.

06:37.054 --> 06:39.925
Lois, all that so-called
evidence has been debunked.

06:39.926 --> 06:41.460
Listen to some of these ingredients:

06:41.461 --> 06:45.466
"mercury, thimerosal,
aluminum, formaldehyde."

06:45.467 --> 06:47.603
Lois, deciding not to vaccinate Stewie

06:47.604 --> 06:48.805
is something that affects all of us.

06:48.806 --> 06:50.140
The only reason they work

06:50.141 --> 06:52.678
is that if a critical mass
of society gets immunized,

06:52.679 --> 06:54.046
then the diseases won't spread.

06:54.047 --> 06:55.883
Look, Brian, I was skeptical, too,

06:55.884 --> 06:57.118
but then I did some research

06:57.119 --> 06:59.121
and I found some very interesting things

06:59.122 --> 07:01.224
from the leader of the
anti-vaccination movement,

07:01.225 --> 07:02.625
Jenny McCarthy.

07:07.602 --> 07:09.070
See? Proof.

07:09.071 --> 07:10.304
Hard to argue with that.

07:10.305 --> 07:11.305
And look at this one.

07:12.943 --> 07:14.412
Glasses.

07:14.413 --> 07:15.913
Case closed.

07:15.914 --> 07:17.316
I can't believe you guys.

07:17.317 --> 07:18.584
Don't you realize you're contributing

07:18.585 --> 07:20.622
to a potential public health disaster

07:20.623 --> 07:22.190
by not vaccinating your child?

07:22.191 --> 07:24.928
That's exactly the point... My child.

07:24.929 --> 07:26.163
He's my child,

07:26.164 --> 07:28.466
and nothing matters more
than his well-being.

07:28.467 --> 07:31.304
Oh, God, this is going to
be a Lois story, isn't it?

07:31.305 --> 07:33.708
<i>Game of Thrones is on, just a reminder.</i>

07:33.709 --> 07:35.577
Yeah, we made this mistake before.

07:35.578 --> 07:37.246
We got the other kids vaccinated,

07:37.247 --> 07:38.850
but Meg still got chicken pox.

07:38.851 --> 07:40.418
Dad, this is acne.

07:40.419 --> 07:41.954
Girl, you nasty.

07:41.955 --> 07:44.691
You realize the vast majority
of people think you're wrong.

07:44.692 --> 07:46.428
Well, maybe that's the problem.

07:46.429 --> 07:48.331
We just got to change their minds.

07:48.332 --> 07:50.301
We're gettin' this town
to change its mind

07:50.302 --> 07:51.470
about vaccinations.

07:51.471 --> 07:52.704
Yeah. I'm with you.

07:52.705 --> 07:54.708
Just as soon as I finish
gettin' the word out

07:54.709 --> 07:56.710
about the one thing more important.

07:56.711 --> 07:59.215
<i>The brothers who made The
Matrix are ladies now!</i>

07:59.216 --> 08:00.282
They're ladies!

08:00.283 --> 08:01.618
Just one of 'em?

08:01.619 --> 08:03.387
That's the thing... It's both of 'em!

08:03.388 --> 08:04.590
What are the chances?

08:04.591 --> 08:06.024
What are the chances?!

08:06.025 --> 08:08.161
<i>The brothers who made The
Matrix are ladies now!</i>

08:13.327 --> 08:14.814
All right, come on, Peter,

08:14.815 --> 08:17.650
I've got all the stuff for
our anti-vaccination rally.

08:17.651 --> 08:18.651
I don't believe this.

08:18.652 --> 08:19.654
It's bad enough you guys

08:19.655 --> 08:20.822
aren't vaccinating Stewie.

08:20.823 --> 08:21.990
Now you're trying to
convince other people

08:21.991 --> 08:23.527
to make the same reckless choice?

08:23.528 --> 08:25.997
I'm also gonna pet a bunch
of dogs without asking.

08:25.998 --> 08:27.366
Don't do that. We don't like that.

08:27.367 --> 08:29.169
Then I'm gonna try and
look at their teeth.

08:29.170 --> 08:32.241
Brian, all we want is for
parents to have the choice.

08:32.242 --> 08:34.810
Because parents know what's
best for their kids.

08:34.811 --> 08:37.614
I hear Sansa finally
shows boob in this one.

08:39.685 --> 08:41.722
You do realize they're
putting your life in danger

08:41.723 --> 08:43.123
by not getting you immunized.

08:43.124 --> 08:45.995
You could get measles, mumps,
rubella, whooping cough...

08:45.996 --> 08:47.296
Oh, my God, are you serious?

08:47.297 --> 08:49.667
Very serious. Even the tiniest germ

08:49.668 --> 08:52.204
could make you very ill and,
left untreated, kill you.

08:52.205 --> 08:53.206
Really?

08:53.207 --> 08:54.208
I'd expect this kind of thing

08:54.209 --> 08:55.943
from the fat man, but not Lois.

08:55.944 --> 08:57.747
Although she did act like a nutcase

08:57.748 --> 09:00.450
that time she went shopping
right before Thanksgiving.

09:00.451 --> 09:02.187
Ready for Turkey Day?

09:02.188 --> 09:03.822
Clever.

09:03.823 --> 09:05.559
Don't eat too much turkey tomorrow.

09:05.560 --> 09:07.728
Oh, I won't.

09:07.729 --> 09:10.433
Now, if only the meal
would cook itself, huh?

09:15.741 --> 09:17.043
Parents of Quahog

09:17.044 --> 09:19.781
and weekend dads playing
three minutes of catch,

09:19.782 --> 09:22.285
do you know that the number
of childhood vaccines

09:22.286 --> 09:24.354
has tripled in the last generation?

09:24.355 --> 09:25.656
And why is that?

09:25.657 --> 09:28.828
Because heartless corporations
make billions of dollars

09:28.829 --> 09:32.233
by foisting garbage and
poison upon our children.

09:36.674 --> 09:38.744
We demand that these vaccines

09:38.745 --> 09:41.448
be tested by independent researchers,

09:41.449 --> 09:43.651
not by the companies who make them.

09:43.652 --> 09:45.854
Excuse me, are you the
lady selling the bullhorn?

09:45.855 --> 09:47.191
What? No.

09:47.192 --> 09:49.293
I'm over here.

09:49.294 --> 09:51.230
Damn it.

09:51.231 --> 09:52.965
This doesn't seem to be working.

09:52.966 --> 09:54.201
Well, obviously, Lois.

09:54.202 --> 09:55.303
You can't just go to a park

09:55.304 --> 09:57.172
and list a bunch of boring facts.

09:57.173 --> 09:58.540
You got to spice things up.

09:58.541 --> 10:00.144
Like I did when I was a lounge singer

10:00.145 --> 10:01.946
with uneven lyric density.

10:01.947 --> 10:05.318
This is a song I wrote for
my beautiful girlfriend.

10:05.319 --> 10:06.453
Her name is...

10:06.454 --> 10:08.390
♪ Kim ♪

10:08.391 --> 10:09.792
♪ I don't understand why your father ♪

10:09.793 --> 10:11.060
♪ Has such problems with us ♪

10:11.061 --> 10:12.897
♪ Kim ♪

10:12.898 --> 10:14.232
♪ Mostly I think it's because ♪

10:14.233 --> 10:15.969
♪ I don't make my car payments on time ♪

10:15.970 --> 10:17.470
♪ But also because I was
dating someone else ♪

10:17.471 --> 10:18.472
♪ At the same time as ♪

10:18.473 --> 10:20.075
♪ Kim ♪

10:20.076 --> 10:21.476
Two, three, four,

10:21.477 --> 10:22.979
five, six, seven, eight,
nine, ten, eleven.

10:22.980 --> 10:24.348
♪ Kim ♪

10:24.349 --> 10:26.084
♪ I love you ♪

10:26.085 --> 10:28.988
♪ But mostly I love that you let
me eat crackers in the bed ♪

10:30.325 --> 10:31.693
♪ Kim! ♪

10:31.694 --> 10:33.329
Thank you!

10:54.796 --> 10:56.398
Eh, that's enough of that.

10:56.399 --> 10:57.499
What the hell?

10:57.500 --> 10:59.336
Peter, is that you on TV right now?

10:59.337 --> 11:02.241
Oh yeah, that's my anti-vaccination PSA.

11:02.242 --> 11:03.843
Hi, I'm a medical guy,

11:03.844 --> 11:07.648
and I'm here to give you
the facts about vaccs.

11:07.649 --> 11:10.620
Fact... Vaccinations cause autism,

11:10.621 --> 11:12.656
paralysis, and even...

11:12.657 --> 11:13.958
death, death, death, death,
death, death, death,

11:13.959 --> 11:15.428
death, death, death.

11:15.429 --> 11:18.666
Fact: "vaccinate" rhymes
with "masturbate."

11:18.667 --> 11:21.337
Would you let a doctor
do that to your kid?

11:21.338 --> 11:25.276
Fact: I still think Michelle
Williams is Carey Mulligan.

11:25.277 --> 11:26.945
Fact!

11:26.946 --> 11:29.849
Medical delivery for
badass karate doctor.

11:29.850 --> 11:32.187
Ah yes, those must be
the bones and skulls.

11:33.924 --> 11:36.828
I see no boob bones,
the victim was a man.

11:36.829 --> 11:37.929
Wow.

11:37.930 --> 11:40.467
♪ Oh, yeah! ♪

11:40.468 --> 11:42.402
<i>Say "no" to vaccines.</i>

11:42.403 --> 11:44.272
<i>Paid for with Meg's college fund.</i>

11:51.284 --> 11:52.686
What the hell is all this?

11:52.687 --> 11:54.721
I'm trying to protect myself
from all those diseases

11:54.722 --> 11:56.425
I'm not vaccinated against.

11:56.426 --> 11:58.728
Speaking of which, do you
have any idea the germs

11:58.729 --> 12:00.932
you routinely track into this house?

12:00.933 --> 12:03.035
From now on I'm going to ask
that you wear these shoes

12:03.036 --> 12:04.036
while indoors.

12:04.037 --> 12:05.105
Where'd you get those?

12:05.106 --> 12:06.307
Put 'em on and lick your lips!

12:06.308 --> 12:08.143
Stewie, you might be
taking this too far.

12:08.144 --> 12:10.480
Proper hygiene depends
on everyone, Brian.

12:10.481 --> 12:12.951
For instance, I've already
saran-wrapped Chris.

12:12.952 --> 12:15.554
I'm a gas station sandwich!

12:17.225 --> 12:19.827
We interrupt this program
with breaking news.

12:19.828 --> 12:22.365
Childhood vaccination rates
in Quahog have dropped

12:22.366 --> 12:25.804
to an all-time low, fueled
by a recent media campaign

12:25.805 --> 12:27.940
led by local meddler, Peter Griffin,

12:27.941 --> 12:31.346
shown here in the basket
of Henry Thomas' bicycle.

12:31.347 --> 12:33.215
That can't be real, right?

12:33.216 --> 12:36.454
Oh, I knew one of these
had to be my house.

12:36.455 --> 12:37.823
Damn it, Peter, thanks to you,

12:37.824 --> 12:40.326
nobody in this town is
vaccinating their kids anymore!

12:40.327 --> 12:42.363
Do you even realize the
harm you've caused?

12:42.364 --> 12:43.698
Harm? What are you talking about?

12:43.699 --> 12:45.433
I'm making the world a better place.

12:45.434 --> 12:47.638
Like when I was the Instagram police.

12:49.708 --> 12:51.376
Sorry, lady, got to crop the chotch.

12:54.550 --> 12:57.786
I... will take this.

12:57.787 --> 12:59.423
And cutaway complete.

13:05.567 --> 13:09.004
Man, there is a lot of bad
art in these hallways.

13:09.005 --> 13:11.909
All right, Stewie, see you after school.

13:11.910 --> 13:14.146
Wait a minute, where are
all the other kids?

13:14.147 --> 13:15.213
Haven't you heard?

13:15.214 --> 13:16.817
There's been an outbreak of measles.

13:16.818 --> 13:19.086
It's all because everyone
stopped vaccinating their kids.

13:19.087 --> 13:20.656
Oh, my God!

13:20.657 --> 13:22.024
And it's not just our school.

13:22.025 --> 13:23.560
Kids all over town are getting sick.

13:25.030 --> 13:26.398
Attention! Attention!

13:26.399 --> 13:28.067
What the hell?

13:32.676 --> 13:34.310
People of Quahog,

13:34.311 --> 13:36.514
your town is under quarantine.

13:36.515 --> 13:40.520
Until further notice, no one
may enter or leave the city.

13:40.521 --> 13:43.458
Oh, that's the guy who bought
the bullhorn at the park.

13:43.459 --> 13:44.927
Oh, this is awful.

13:44.928 --> 13:46.429
It's all our fault!

13:46.430 --> 13:48.099
And look, Joe's arguing
with a state policeman

13:48.100 --> 13:49.668
over jurisdiction.

13:49.669 --> 13:51.738
Thanks, Swanson, we'll
take it from here.

13:51.739 --> 13:53.073
It's a state matter now.

13:53.074 --> 13:55.043
No way, this is my town.

13:55.044 --> 13:57.213
Thanks, guys, the feds
will take it from here.

13:57.214 --> 13:59.282
Oh, no, this is my state.

13:59.283 --> 14:01.420
Hi, I'm a crossing guard who can walk,

14:01.421 --> 14:03.790
so I have jurisdiction over all of you.

14:03.791 --> 14:05.326
Must be serious.

14:05.327 --> 14:07.074
They brought in the big guns.

14:12.983 --> 14:14.085
You happy now, Lois?

14:14.086 --> 14:15.887
Because of you, there's
a measles epidemic,

14:15.888 --> 14:17.489
and the whole town is quarantined.

14:17.490 --> 14:18.892
Speak for yourself, Brian.

14:18.893 --> 14:22.030
I, for one, am enjoying
the indoor family time.

14:22.031 --> 14:24.967
Who's up for another game
of hot-breath telephone?

14:26.939 --> 14:28.640
We're all gonna die!

14:28.641 --> 14:30.777
Chris, you're supposed to whisper
that to the next person.

14:30.778 --> 14:32.280
Peter, Brian's right!

14:32.281 --> 14:33.748
We were wrong about everything!

14:33.749 --> 14:36.586
We've got to get to the hospital
and get Stewie vaccinated!

14:36.587 --> 14:38.456
Eh, it might be a little
too late for that.

14:38.457 --> 14:41.327
I kind of destroyed all
the vaccines in town.

15:04.865 --> 15:06.700
All right, what else did
I have to do today?

15:06.701 --> 15:08.669
Ah, yes, overdose in my apartment.

15:08.670 --> 15:10.239
I better get home.

15:10.240 --> 15:12.475
You destroyed all the vaccines?

15:12.476 --> 15:14.612
Yeah, but it's fine. There's
nothing to worry about.

15:14.613 --> 15:16.549
Is anyone else feeling feverish, achy,

15:16.550 --> 15:18.217
and acutely sensitive to light?

15:18.218 --> 15:19.586
Oh, my God, Peter.

15:19.587 --> 15:21.256
Y-you've got measles!

15:21.257 --> 15:23.793
Now, hold on, hold on,
before we all freak out,

15:23.794 --> 15:25.496
it might just be full-body herpes.

15:25.497 --> 15:28.267
Wait, you guys, Dad might
not have been vaccinated.

15:28.268 --> 15:30.136
Didn't Grandma say he
was born in Mexico?

15:30.137 --> 15:31.539
Nobody remembers that, Meg.

15:31.540 --> 15:33.542
We got to keep you away from Stewie.

15:33.543 --> 15:34.644
You'll get him sick.

15:34.645 --> 15:36.446
Oh, my little guy's gonna be fine.

15:36.447 --> 15:38.183
All he needs is a good,
old-fashioned game

15:38.184 --> 15:40.118
of hot-breath telephone.

15:40.119 --> 15:41.421
Measles.

15:41.422 --> 15:42.956
I've got to get out of this house,

15:42.957 --> 15:45.527
or I'll be in worse shape
than John Goodman!

15:45.528 --> 15:47.030
I've got your EKG here.

15:47.031 --> 15:48.198
How does it look?

15:48.199 --> 15:50.368
Well, it spells out "Pancakes."

15:50.369 --> 15:52.771
Oh, okay, so same as last time.

15:52.772 --> 15:55.876
I'm recommending you go on
a strict diet immediately.

15:55.877 --> 15:57.145
Nope.

15:57.146 --> 15:58.981
Horses that make it
look like I can walk,

15:58.982 --> 16:00.883
take me to Hollywood!

16:09.832 --> 16:11.734
All right, I'm almost done packing.

16:11.735 --> 16:14.304
I've got it down to
four bags and a hatbox.

16:14.305 --> 16:15.641
I'm gonna need some help, Rupert.

16:15.642 --> 16:16.742
Rupert?

16:16.743 --> 16:19.914
Ew, that's the tushie thermometer.

16:19.915 --> 16:21.984
Dear God, you're burning up!

16:21.985 --> 16:23.185
I have to get out of here!

16:24.923 --> 16:26.323
I'm sorry, Rupert.

16:26.324 --> 16:28.494
But the situation here
has become unbearable.

16:28.495 --> 16:31.366
Like talking to someone
with adult braces.

16:31.367 --> 16:33.568
So, yeah, last weekend,
Sheila and I took the kids

16:33.569 --> 16:35.037
up to the lake, it was great.

16:35.038 --> 16:37.708
We had great weather,
fired up the barbecue,

16:37.709 --> 16:39.678
Sheila's parents came up
towards the end of the week...

16:39.679 --> 16:42.047
When are you gonna get those off?

16:46.690 --> 16:49.827
Meg, you must carry on my legacy.

16:49.828 --> 16:53.199
Promise me you'll crop the chotches.

16:53.200 --> 16:54.634
Crop them, Meg!

16:54.635 --> 16:55.870
Crop them all!

16:55.871 --> 16:57.673
Peter, Stewie's gone!

16:57.674 --> 16:59.208
I've looked everywhere!

16:59.209 --> 17:01.946
Oh, Lois, I feel a little better.

17:01.947 --> 17:03.915
I think I could keep down deviled eggs.

17:03.916 --> 17:04.917
Lois, what's wrong?

17:04.918 --> 17:06.353
I can't find Stewie.

17:06.354 --> 17:08.121
He must've gotten out of the house.

17:08.122 --> 17:10.759
God knows how far he's gone.

17:10.760 --> 17:13.598
<i>Well, look, there's a
 Family Circus dotted path.</i>

17:13.599 --> 17:14.799
It'll lead us right to him.

17:19.608 --> 17:20.942
Ah, it's just Billy.

17:20.943 --> 17:22.511
He died of measles.

17:22.512 --> 17:25.950
And here comes Marmaduke
to lick up the vomit.

17:25.951 --> 17:27.719
Lucky.

17:31.760 --> 17:33.528
If I can just escape this quarantine

17:33.529 --> 17:34.697
and make it to the next town,

17:34.698 --> 17:37.901
I'll be able to get that vaccine I need.

17:37.902 --> 17:39.905
Stewie! I'm you from the future!

17:39.906 --> 17:42.309
You've got to get the hell out
of town before you get sick!

17:42.310 --> 17:44.145
Yeah, I know. That's what I'm doing.

17:44.146 --> 17:46.382
Okay, I'm really here because
I know you have glue.

17:46.383 --> 17:48.785
Give me the glue.

17:51.958 --> 17:53.192
Stewie, listen to me,

17:53.193 --> 17:56.280
never, ever do this great thing I love.

18:04.177 --> 18:06.445
There's the bridge out of town!

18:08.818 --> 18:10.519
So we're all there at the Clam,

18:10.520 --> 18:12.389
just kind of making music together,

18:12.390 --> 18:14.559
and then Peter, of
course, had to join in

18:14.560 --> 18:18.265
and clap his hands, and I said,
"Eh, that's enough of that."

18:18.266 --> 18:20.535
Yeah, I kind of run the group.

18:22.472 --> 18:24.074
I'll just have to go around them.

18:31.886 --> 18:33.189
Good Lord.

18:33.190 --> 18:35.091
I hope my shoe doesn't
fall to make me realize

18:35.092 --> 18:36.358
how far the drop is.

18:41.135 --> 18:44.004
Oh, my orthotic was in there.

18:45.776 --> 18:47.276
Stewie?

18:47.277 --> 18:48.277
Where are you?

18:48.278 --> 18:50.148
Lois, what's going on?

18:50.149 --> 18:52.118
That's one of my sidekicks' wives.

18:52.119 --> 18:54.154
He says he's in charge of
the group, is that true?

18:54.155 --> 18:57.058
No, not in the slightest, but,
Joe, Stewie's gone missing.

18:57.059 --> 18:58.795
We can't find him anywhere.

18:58.796 --> 19:00.295
Lois, look!

19:03.669 --> 19:05.471
I don't know if he can
hold on much longer.

19:05.472 --> 19:06.473
We got to get him down.

19:06.474 --> 19:07.909
Stewie, hang on!

19:07.910 --> 19:09.110
Mommy's coming!

19:12.617 --> 19:15.888
Oh, no, upside-down train!

19:17.925 --> 19:19.426
- Stewie!
- Oh, no!

19:24.702 --> 19:26.036
Sean Penn?

19:26.037 --> 19:28.374
That's right, two-time
Oscar winner Sean Penn.

19:28.375 --> 19:29.743
What are you doing here?

19:29.744 --> 19:32.213
I'm bringing vaccines into
your quarantined town.

19:32.214 --> 19:34.817
Any time there's a public health
crisis in a third-world land,

19:34.818 --> 19:35.886
I'm there.

19:35.887 --> 19:37.688
Third world? This is Rhode Island.

19:37.689 --> 19:38.957
Oh, really?

19:38.958 --> 19:40.993
Have you seen some of the
delis on Federal Hill?

19:40.994 --> 19:42.663
Oh-ho-ho! Rhode Island slam!

19:42.664 --> 19:45.667
Ho-ho! I like you, Sean Penn.

19:47.204 --> 19:50.041
Oh, my God, you saved my baby!

19:50.042 --> 19:52.779
Thank you so mu... Oh.

19:52.780 --> 19:54.682
Sean Penn.

19:54.683 --> 19:56.961
You're the one who
played that homosexual.

19:56.962 --> 19:57.720
Yeah.

19:57.721 --> 19:59.922
All right, well, I'll take my son now.

19:59.923 --> 20:02.360
I've brought enough vaccines
for your whole town.

20:02.361 --> 20:04.264
I hope you've realized
that vaccinations are not

20:04.265 --> 20:07.201
a freedom of choice issue,
they're a public health issue.

20:07.202 --> 20:10.673
Thanks to them, countless
serious diseases, mumps, polio,

20:10.674 --> 20:13.612
smallpox, and rubella, have
been all but eradicated.

20:13.613 --> 20:15.614
Like clean water and functional schools,

20:15.615 --> 20:18.118
vaccinations are a human right.

20:18.119 --> 20:21.590
Great, just what I needed, a
lecture from liberal Hollywood.

20:21.591 --> 20:25.630
This whole thing has been a
lecture from liberal Hollywood.

20:29.471 --> 20:31.806
Well, it's a relief that
everyone's been vaccinated,

20:31.807 --> 20:33.342
and the quarantine has been lifted.

20:33.343 --> 20:35.412
Well, I'm just happy
that Stewie is healthy,

20:35.413 --> 20:38.951
and only 150 people died, but
not anyone we knew personally.

20:38.952 --> 20:41.421
Yeah, I know I sure learned something.

20:42.624 --> 20:44.767
Hey, do you like apples?

20:44.768 --> 20:46.129
Yeah.

20:46.130 --> 20:47.431
Well, I got her number.

20:47.432 --> 20:48.799
How do you like them apples?

20:48.800 --> 20:50.185
Oh, Bat Damon!

20:50.186 --> 20:52.106
You got the best of me again!

20:52.107 --> 20:53.107
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru